course: dictionary
lesson: 12310
title: Corpulence and describing bodies kindly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Corpulence is a formal word for being very fat or heavy in the body. You will mostly meet it in old books and in serious or medical writing, not in everyday chat.
explain: «The old writer described the greedy squire and his great corpulence.» The clues are greedy and great. They suggest the squire's body is very large, so corpulence must mean being very fat or heavy.
explain: Today, health lessons more often say «obesity» or «being overweight». Corpulence describes a body rather than insulting it, but talking about someone's body can still hurt them, so choose your words kindly.
fact: Corpulence is a noun, a thing you can name, like sadness or height.
fact: Corpulence means being very fat or heavy in the body.
fact: It is a formal or old-fashioned word, found in old stories and medical writing.
fact: Today people often say «overweight» or «obesity» instead.
fact: Describing someone's body can hurt their feelings, so think kindly before you use such words.
exercise: «The old story described the greedy squire and his great corpulence.» What does corpulence mean? | Being very quick on your feet | Being very tall and thin | Being very rich and happy | *Being very fat or heavy in the body
exercise: Which word do health lessons use today instead of corpulence? | *Obesity | Cheerful | Hungry | Tired
exercise: Corpulence is which kind of word? | A word for places | A word for colours | Quick, everyday chat | *Formal or old-fashioned
test: What part of speech is corpulence? | An adjective, like happy | An adverb, like quickly | A verb, like run | *A noun, like sadness
test: Why should we think kindly before using words like corpulence about someone? | *Because talking about someone's body can hurt their feelings | Because it means being very clever | Because it is always a compliment | Because it is only used for animals
exam: Which sentence uses corpulence correctly? | *The old painting showed a jolly monk of great corpulence. | Corpulence was the colour of the sky. | She ran corpulence across the field. | The corpulence rode a bicycle to school.
